# Trademond Dashboard — Admin UI

**Purpose**: Web admin dashboard for the Trademond platform — manages products, services, companies, users, plans, features, subscriptions, sponsorships, experiments, and related workflows.

- **Package name**: `trademond-dashboard`
- **Base URL**: derived from `VITE_API_BASE_URL` (default `https://trademond.net/api/v1`)

## Tech Stack
| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Framework | React 19 + TypeScript (strict mode) |
| Bundler | Vite (with `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin) |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui |
| Routing | react-router-dom v7 |
| Server State | TanStack React Query v5 |
| Forms | react-hook-form + yup validation |
| HTTP Client | Axios (custom `axiosClient` with JWT interceptor) |
| i18n | react-i18next (Arabic RTL + English LTR) |
| Notifications | sonner |
| Icons | lucide-react |
| Charts | recharts |
| Utilities | clsx + tailwind-merge via `cn()` helper |

## Key Conventions
- All user-facing text must use `react-i18next` — call `t()` for every visible string.
- The app supports **RTL** (Arabic) and **LTR** (English) — use logical CSS properties (`ms-`, `me-`, `ps-`, `pe-`, `start-`, `end-`) instead of physical (`ml-`, `mr-`, `left-`, `right-`).
- Authentication uses **JWT tokens** stored in `localStorage`. The Axios interceptor attaches the token automatically.
- API bilingual data uses `BilingualText` type — render it with `displayBilingual()` from `@utils/ui`.
- Environment variables are prefixed with `VITE_` and accessed via `import.meta.env`.
